# Day 7 - Claude Usage Strategy

## Overview

Today I learned how to use Claude more strategically by selecting the right model and effort level based on the task.

Instead of using the same settings for everything, I explored when to use Haiku, Sonnet, and Opus, and how effort levels can improve output quality.

---

## My Profile

- Student (B.Tech CSE - AI & ML)
- Python Learner
- Aspiring AI Engineer
- Content Creator
- Project Builder

---

## Recommended Primary Model

### Claude Sonnet

Why?

- Best balance of speed and accuracy
- Excellent for coding and learning
- Great for project planning
- Suitable for daily use

---

## When to Use Haiku

- Quick summaries
- Caption generation
- Brainstorming ideas
- Simple questions
- Fast responses

### Best Effort
Low / Standard

---

## When to Use Sonnet

- Learning AI/ML concepts
- Python coding
- DSA preparation
- Resume improvement
- Interview preparation
- Project documentation

### Best Effort
Standard / High

---

## When to Use Opus

- Deep research
- Startup planning
- Complex project architecture
- Multi-step reasoning
- Strategic decision-making

### Best Effort
High / Max

---

## Recommended Effort Levels

### Low
- Quick tasks
- Summaries
- Captions

### Standard (Default)
- Daily learning
- Coding help
- Project work
- Career guidance

### High
- Research
- System design
- Project planning

### Max
- Critical decisions
- Advanced reasoning
- Large-scale project strategy

---

## My Personalized Workflow

| Task | Model | Effort |
|--------|--------|--------|
| Learning AI/ML | Sonnet | Standard |
| Python Practice | Sonnet | Standard |
| DSA Preparation | Sonnet | Standard |
| Resume Building | Sonnet | High |
| Interview Preparation | Sonnet | High |
| Project Planning | Opus | High |
| LinkedIn Captions | Haiku | Low |
| Instagram Content | Haiku | Low |
| Documentation | Sonnet | Standard |

---

## Key Learnings

- The best AI model depends on the task.
- More effort does not always mean better results.
- Providing context improves output quality.
- Claude can be used as a tutor, coding assistant, mentor, and productivity partner.
- A structured workflow helps maximize AI effectiveness.

---

## Final Recommendation

If I could use only one model and one effort level:

**Model:** Claude Sonnet

**Effort:** Standard

Reason:
It offers the best balance of speed, reasoning, quality, and efficiency for most of my daily tasks as an AI & ML student.
